<!-- snippets/jc-buybox-sizes.liquid -->
{% comment %}
  "STEP 1 · HOW MANY" — the size tile row, plus the free shipping bar beneath it.

  The tiles themselves are unchanged apart from what was taken off them: the
  per-tile shipping lines (now the one bar below) and the "Best Value" badge
  (now the hero savings sentence). The .jc-bb-sizes wrapper is what holds the
  row to four across at every width; see attomik-custom.css.

  Accepts:
  - block: {object} The variant_cards block.

  Usage:
    {% render 'jc-buybox-sizes', block: block %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  The step label is tied to the same condition product__variant-cards.liquid
  uses to decide whether to render at all. On a single-variant product there is
  no size to choose, and a "STEP 1 · HOW MANY" heading over an empty row would
  announce a control that is not there. The shipping bar still renders — free
  shipping is about the price, not about having a choice of packs.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign has_sizes = true
  if product.has_only_default_variant or product.options_with_values.size == 0
    assign has_sizes = false
  endif
-%}

<div class="jc-bb-sizes w-full">
  {% if has_sizes %}
    <span class="jc-bb-step">Step 1 &middot; How many</span>
    {% render 'product__variant-cards', block: block, hide_option_label: true %}
  {% endif %}
  {% render 'jc-buybox-shipping' %}
</div>
